  (text "@ (, 200, 306) mA" (exclude_from_sim no) (at 139.7 67.31 0) (effects (font (size 1.27 1.27)) (justify left top)) (uuid "3f1ee505-424f-5143-b8fd-7bcdda641074"))
  (text "U201 TPS2553DBV (active-high EN, auto-retry). Why a switch here:" (exclude_from_sim no) (at 20.32 104.14 0) (effects (font (size 1.27 1.27)) (justify left top)) (uuid "01e34637-61f9-5aed-b7a1-391ab5be73a4"))
  (text " - inrush: USB allows 10 uF at plug-in; the chain has 82 x 100 nF + 470 uF bulk (C984), so it is charged at the current limit;" (exclude_from_sim no) (at 20.32 106.68 0) (effects (font (size 1.27 1.27)) (justify left top)) (uuid "05f2579d-907f-5dbf-8261-f5d0e05ada28"))
  (text " - backstop: a firmware error that lights the whole grid at full white (82 x 60 mA) cannot pull more than 306 mA;" (exclude_from_sim no) (at 20.32 109.22 0) (effects (font (size 1.27 1.27)) (justify left top)) (uuid "c65b0135-057b-5cd4-98e6-7c46b8720d9e"))
  (text " - power-up: EN follows +3V3 (threshold 0.66-1.1 V), so the rail comes up with the Pico's regulator, before the firmware runs." (exclude_from_sim no) (at 20.32 111.76 0) (effects (font (size 1.27 1.27)) (justify left top)) (uuid "c20b703d-a529-5a59-8d4d-18bac5336975"))
  (text "R201 100 kOhm 1% sets the limit, IOS = (232, 267, 306) mA with the 1 % tolerance (TPS2553 eq. 1-3). Firmware budget 200 mA;" (exclude_from_sim no) (at 20.32 114.3 0) (effects (font (size 1.27 1.27)) (justify left top)) (uuid "833ff30a-7794-58f2-87cf-192b3b824752"))
  (text "keep R201 >= 82 kOhm (IOS max 369 mA). The 5 V budget below is an estimate until the OLED is chosen and the board measured." (exclude_from_sim no) (at 20.32 116.84 0) (effects (font (size 1.27 1.27)) (justify left top)) (uuid "b470003e-8556-5463-b350-78f3b50be752"))
  (text "TP201: low while U201 limits current or is too hot. Large capacitors sit behind U201; on VBUS only C201, C504/C505/C507 (sheet 5)." (exclude_from_sim no) (at 20.32 119.38 0) (effects (font (size 1.27 1.27)) (justify left top)) (uuid "94060b1b-eefa-5492-abdf-59dbc6cd3ae9"))
  (text "JP201 (EN source): 1-2 bridged by copper = rail follows +3V3, as designed. Cut 1-2 and bridge 2-3 to let GPIO 7 switch" (exclude_from_sim no) (at 20.32 121.92 0) (effects (font (size 1.27 1.27)) (justify left top)) (uuid "9601d5c6-7e98-58f6-a173-abe0a2b1aa95"))
  (text "the rail after USB enumeration (R203 keeps it off until then); GPIO 7 is then no longer the jitter probe (TP301)." (exclude_from_sim no) (at 20.32 124.46 0) (effects (font (size 1.27 1.27)) (justify left top)) (uuid "ed2458ef-038b-5e6b-8803-84de83e58312"))
  (text "+5V_LED min 4.7 V is VBUS min minus the switch (~30 mV at 200 mA); it falls lower only while U201 limits current." (exclude_from_sim no) (at 20.32 127 0) (effects (font (size 1.27 1.27)) (justify left top)) (uuid "210a6192-a41a-535c-8bdf-a1180e0a9112"))
  (text "Rails and budget" (exclude_from_sim no) (at 20.32 139.7 0) (effects (font (size 2.54 2.54) (thickness 0.508) (bold yes)) (justify left bottom)) (uuid "9c66f22c-d873-549d-8cf7-4053d0f9f6af"))
  (text "VBUS    5 V from USB, Pico pin 40. Loads: U201 (LED chain), U503 MCP6004, U504 74AHCT125, Pico VSYS (through its own diode)." (exclude_from_sim no) (at 20.32 146.05 0) (effects (font (size 1.27 1.27)) (justify left top)) (uuid "a1a4ee69-270b-509e-8ac7-d269ef72f2b7"))
  (text "+3V3    Pico's RT6150B buck-boost, pin 36; external load <= 300 mA (Pico datasheet), this board ~100 mA:" (exclude_from_sim no) (at 20.32 148.59 0) (effects (font (size 1.27 1.27)) (justify left top)) (uuid "2ebd1115-48be-5d29-ab79-4290751a82c5"))
  (text "        OLED ~25 mA, step LEDs 16 x 3 mA, MIDI OUT 7 mA, five expanders, DACs, pull-ups." (exclude_from_sim no) (at 20.32 151.13 0) (effects (font (size 1.27 1.27)) (justify left top)) (uuid "c92af0fe-490d-5bc6-963a-cee6ea80467a"))
  (text "+5V_LED switched VBUS for the RGB chain only (sheet 9)." (exclude_from_sim no) (at 20.32 153.67 0) (effects (font (size 1.27 1.27)) (justify left top)) (uuid "c3195a83-d035-5cbb-af0f-2249e2964ee4"))
  (text "GND     one ground. On the board, return the LED-chain current to the Pico's GND pins on its own path," (exclude_from_sim no) (at 20.32 156.21 0) (effects (font (size 1.27 1.27)) (justify left top)) (uuid "8795b3c7-6a6d-5963-92ee-662d6ce7effc"))
  (text "        apart from the DAC/op-amp ground of sheet 5 (CV noise check in HARDWARE_STATUS.md)." (exclude_from_sim no) (at 20.32 158.75 0) (effects (font (size 1.27 1.27)) (justify left top)) (uuid "223b0c3f-54bd-5cec-92cf-44ea611b4333"))
  (text "Budget at 5 V (estimate): RGB chain <= 200 mA (firmware) / 306 mA (U201), Pico + 3.3 V loads 100-130 mA through the" (exclude_from_sim no) (at 20.32 161.29 0) (effects (font (size 1.27 1.27)) (justify left top)) (uuid "13680e85-b5e5-562e-a309-a62d95760708"))
  (text "buck-boost, gates <= 20 mA => about 450 mA worst case. Idle: 82 x ~1 mA for the chain plus the Pico, above the 100 mA" (exclude_from_sim no) (at 20.32 163.83 0) (effects (font (size 1.27 1.27)) (justify left top)) (uuid "e17c1e64-45db-55d4-8f4f-af0200728ca6"))
  (text "an unconfigured USB device may draw; most laptop ports allow it (design: bench on two laptops)." (exclude_from_sim no) (at 20.32 166.37 0) (effects (font (size 1.27 1.27)) (justify left top)) (uuid "f30fe8d5-7a8c-5c9b-b118-1751719d2708"))
  (label "LED_EN" (at 66.04 66.04 180) (effects (font (size 1.27 1.27)) (justify right bottom)) (uuid "7b9533e4-1c10-5936-bc69-a8af3befd91f"))
  (label "LED_EN" (at 35.56 69.85 0) (effects (font (size 1.27 1.27)) (justify left bottom)) (uuid "3b63b799-cf9c-529c-bd35-e855778be3af"))
  (hierarchical_label "JITTER_PROBE" (shape bidirectional) (at 27.94 76.2 180) (effects (font (size 1.27 1.27)) (justify right)) (uuid "7f59a62d-2ffb-5f7e-822a-2405e6315488"))
